EXPERIMENT 12: Policy-Based Reinforcement Learning for Industrial Robotic Arm
Aim

To implement a policy-based Reinforcement Learning model for an industrial robotic arm to perform efficient pick-and-place operations.

Algorithm / Procedure
Define the robotic arm states.
Define possible arm movements as actions.
Create a policy neural network.
Generate actions according to the learned policy.
Calculate rewards based on successful pick-and-place operations.
Update the policy using the obtained rewards.
Repeat the process for multiple training episodes.
Select the action with the highest probability.
Program
import numpy as np
from tensorflow.keras.models import Sequential
from tensorflow.keras.layers import Dense


model = Sequential([
    Dense(16, activation="relu", input_shape=(3,)),
    Dense(16, activation="relu"),
    Dense(3, activation="softmax")
])


model.compile(optimizer="adam", loss="categorical_crossentropy")


states = np.array([
    [0, 0, 1],
    [1, 0, 1],
    [1, 1, 0],
    [0, 1, 1]
])


actions = np.array([
    [1, 0, 0],
    [0, 1, 0],
    [0, 0, 1],
    [1, 0, 0]
])


model.fit(states, actions, epochs=50, verbose=0)


probabilities = model.predict(states, verbose=0)


print("Policy Training Completed")
print("\nAction Probabilities:")
print(np.round(probabilities, 2))


print("\nSelected Actions:")
print(np.argmax(probabilities, axis=1))
